# Meta Marketing API credentials.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored and must
# NEVER be committed — this repository is public, and a leaked ad-account token
# is picked up by automated scanners within minutes.
#
# In production this is set in Vercel: Project -> Settings -> Environment
# Variables. Vercel reads it at deploy time, so after adding or changing it you
# must redeploy for it to take effect.

# The ONLY required value. System User token with the ads_read scope ONLY.
#
# ads_read is read-only: if this token leaked it could expose your numbers but
# could not spend money or change campaigns. Never grant ads_management.
#
# Paste the token into Vercel's env var field or this local .env file — never
# into source code, a commit, a terminal command, or a chat message.
META_ACCESS_TOKEN=

# Optional. The ad account is already set in api/meta.ts, because an account ID
# is configuration rather than a credential — it is visible in Ads Manager URLs
# and is useless without a token authorised for it. Set this only to point the
# dashboard at a different account.
# META_AD_ACCOUNT_ID=act_1354995341608155

# NOT USED, and deliberately so:
#   App ID     — public by design, safe to expose, but this dashboard does not need it.
#   App Secret — highly sensitive. It can mint tokens for your app. It has no place
#                in this project. If yours has ever been shared, reset it at
#                developers.facebook.com -> your app -> Settings -> Basic.
